2. two site irreps at one position the invariants do not distinguish
   (B2) at d        : theta_Z = (1, 0, 1, 1, 1, -1, 0)   theta_Zn = {2: (0, 0, 1)}
   (B3) at d        : theta_Z = (1, 0, 1, 1, 1, -1, 0)   theta_Zn = {2: (0, 0, 1)}
   the pair         : B2 / B3 at Wyckoff d, the EBRs B2↑G(6) and B3↑G(6)
   both members induce the same symmetry-data vector and carry identical
   SRSIs, so neither a momentum-space nor a real-space measurement
   separates them.

3. SG 147 without SOC: printed indicator rows that are not indicators
   the tables       : #147.14, tabulated indicators z2,3 (mod 2), z4 (mod 4)
   the test case    : (Au) at a, EBR column 3 of #147.14 -- an atomic limit, so
                      every indicator must read 0 on it
   theta            : (0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
   the printed rows : z2,3 = 1 mod 2, z4 = 2 mod 4
   what is returned : {'z2,3': 0, 'z4': 0}, the derived rows
   over all systems : 390 tabulated indicator rows -- 374 equal, 9 with no derived row, 4 different, 3 equivalent
   the different    : #147.14 z2,3, #147.14 z4, #162.74 z2', #163.80 z2' -- and nothing else
   the rows returned are the derived ones, which vanish on every elementary
   band representation; the printed rows are kept beside them.

4. the symmetry-indicated split EBRs, re-asked with a full enumeration
   the list         : 211 splittings, 9 without SOC and 202 with, 203 of them marked SRSI-mismatching
   the supplement's mismatch column, recomputed here from the theta rows beside it, agrees on 211 of 211.
   the criterion, with H the parent EBR, V the first child and C the rest:
      the mark    valuedness  verdict                     count
      flagged     double      diagnosed topological       193
      flagged     double      invisible to the SRSIs      1
      flagged     single      diagnosed topological       9
      unflagged   double      invisible to the SRSIs      5
      unflagged   double      no Z_n SRSIs                3
   the headline     : 202 of the 203 flagged splittings stay diagnosed topological
   the exception    : #209.49  (-1F2F)_c -> -F@a + -F@b   'invisible to the SRSIs', 2 consistent pairs
   a consistent pair is two atomic realizations, one per side, whose Z_n-SRSIs
   add up to the total's; where one exists, the splitting's topology is
   invisible to the invariants.
   the 8 unflagged splittings, one by one:
      #202.23   (-1F2F)_c    -> -1Fg2Fg@a + -1Fu2Fu@a  'invisible to the SRSIs' (1 consistent pair)
      #202.23   (-1F2F)_c    -> -1Fg2Fg@b + -1Fu2Fu@b  'invisible to the SRSIs' (1 consistent pair)
      #209.49   (-1F2F)_c    -> -F@a + -F@a            'invisible to the SRSIs' (2 consistent pairs)
      #209.49   (-1F2F)_c    -> -F@b + -F@b            'invisible to the SRSIs' (2 consistent pairs)
      #211.57   (-1E2E)_c    -> -F@a + -F@a            'invisible to the SRSIs' (1 consistent pair)
      #223.105  (-1E2E)_e    -> -1Fg2Fg@a + -1Fu2Fu@a  'no Z_n SRSIs' (1 consistent pair)
      #225.117  (-F)_c       -> -Fg@a + -Fu@a          'no Z_n SRSIs' (1 consistent pair)
      #225.117  (-F)_c       -> -Fg@b + -Fu@b          'no Z_n SRSIs' (1 consistent pair)
   the 3 'no Z_n SRSIs' entries are groups whose SRSI group has no Z_n row, so there is no additivity to test.

